# Where the student portal (student-frontend) is served from. The public
# platform links into it for login, registration and the dashboard, and hands
# a student's anonymous research across in the URL fragment.
#
# Local development — the CRA portal's default port:
#   NEXT_PUBLIC_PORTAL_URL=http://localhost:3000
#
# Omitted, it falls back to the hosted dashboard (see lib/config.ts).
NEXT_PUBLIC_PORTAL_URL=http://localhost:3000

# --- Contact widget (phone + WhatsApp) ---
# The floating widget on every page. `CONTACT_PHONE` keeps its `+` so `tel:`
# dials correctly from abroad; `CONTACT_WHATSAPP` is digits only with the
# country code and no `+`, which is the form wa.me requires. The committed
# defaults are placeholders — set these before any deploy that real students
# will see.
NEXT_PUBLIC_CONTACT_PHONE=+442080000000
NEXT_PUBLIC_CONTACT_WHATSAPP=442080000000
NEXT_PUBLIC_CONTACT_HOURS=Mon–Fri, 9am–6pm UK time

# --- Lead capture ---
# Where the homepage callback form POSTs its JSON {name, email, phone,
# newsletter, stage, submittedAt}. Left unset, the form keeps the submission
# in the student's browser and reports success without transmitting anything,
# so local development and preview builds work without a backend.
# NEXT_PUBLIC_LEAD_ENDPOINT=https://example.com/api/leads

# --- CMS: publish invalidation and draft preview ---
# Shared with the admin API's LANDING_REVALIDATE_SECRET. Both halves need the
# same value: the backend signs preview tokens and authenticates its cache
# purges with it, and /api/revalidate and /api/preview verify against it.
#
# Server-only — never prefix this NEXT_PUBLIC_. Left unset, both endpoints
# refuse rather than default open, and the site falls back to its ordinary
# revalidation timers.
REVALIDATE_SECRET=

# --- Ignition API ---
# Where the backend serves the public catalogue and CMS content from. Every
# university, course, scholarship, guide and article on this site is read from
# here at build and revalidation time; the files under data/ are only the
# fallback used when it cannot be reached.
#
# Local development — the Ignition backend's offset port (ED360 occupies 8000
# on the same machine):
NEXT_PUBLIC_API_BASE_URL=http://localhost:8001/api/v1
